<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_31" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_31">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_31" name="BPMN-31 | Saved Delivery Address Maintenance" processRef="Process_31" />
    <bpmn:participant id="Maps_35" name="Google Maps Platform — address search and validation" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="MapsRequest_35" sourceRef="MapsLookup_35" targetRef="Maps_35" name="Address search/validation request" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="MapsResponse_35" sourceRef="Maps_35" targetRef="MapsLookup_35" name="Address/location result when available" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_31" name="Saved Delivery Address Maintenance" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-31 and all catalog boundaries; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.4 FR-ADDR-01-05 and stimulus/response support for editing/removing addresses; supporting NFR-SEC-03-04,08, NFR-REL-01-04. Website: index.html loads app/address-state.js R.active/find/save/archive/setDefault/defaults/changed, app/account.js saved-address forms/remove confirmation, app/address-map.js static preview, and app/commerce-ui.js address editor. SRS governs: proposed system integrates Maps search/location validation, unlike preview static image/city checks. No provider-specific endpoint, response field, coordinate precision or delivery radius is invented. Scope: authenticated customer maintains own multiple labeled saved addresses and one default. BPMN-26 owns sign-in; authorization/record ownership rechecked here. Customer/System are internal descriptive responsibility lanes; Google Maps is a black-box external participant connected only by message flows. Local validation and unsuccessful outcomes are visible; no embedded collapsed subprocess or generic broadcast event. Inputs: authenticated customer, requested create/edit/remove/default action, optional selected address and input draft. Multiple addresses retain distinct identities; modifying one must not replace the entire address book. FR-ADDR-05 is downstream reuse: BPMN-02 loads/selects saved addresses during purchase; BPMN-18 rechecks courier eligibility/fees, not called by address maintenance. Saving an address is not courier service-area approval. Existing paid/confirmed purchase delivery snapshots and subscription commitments remain unchanged, including BR-26; draft address selections may be invalidated/refreshed by implementation. Maps validation is required for new or changed location data, not setting default/removing an already saved address or editing only its label. Default policy follows prototype: at most one active default; the first saved address becomes default, and if default is removed another remaining active address is chosen using the supported fallback (prototype earliest created). Removing last address leaves empty book/no default. This fallback is an implementation choice, not an extra user approval requirement. Customer may explicitly designate another saved default. Failed combined saves preserve current saved records/default; no unrelated account or purchase modification. No checkout, courier booking/payment, external notice, inventory or owner allocation is performed. BPMN-17 remains partially reviewed by the user.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_31">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_35_customer" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Edit_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Confirm_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Cancel_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>MapsPending_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>ChooseMapsRetry_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>RetryMaps_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>ViewUpdated_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_35_system" name="Kitchen406 System — Delivery Address Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Load_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Validate_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Valid_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>InputError_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>LocationChanged_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>MapsLookup_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>MapsResult_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>LocationError_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>MapsError_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Save_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Saved_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>SaveError_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>SaveEnd_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Show_35</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_35" name="Customer opens saved-address maintenance">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Load_35" name="Load saved address book">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-ADDR-01. Load the signed-in customer’s saved addresses, labels and default. An empty address book is valid. Sign-in is handled in BPMN-26.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Edit_35" name="Add/edit a labeled address, choose a default, remove an address or leave">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-ADDR-01-03. Select action and owned address where applicable. Add/edit captures applicable address/location information, label and optional default choice. Address search assistance is provided by the Maps task later in the flow; customer can correct/retry rejected input. Remove shows confirmation; default selects an existing saved record. Leaving cancels maintenance. No fixed address count, uniqueness of labels or administrative approval is imposed by the SRS.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_RetryYes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Confirm_35" name="Customer submits/confirms the change?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Cancel_35" name="No changes submitted; saved book retained">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Validate_35" name="Validate action, owned record and applicable address fields">
      <bpmn:documentation>NFR-SEC-04,08. Recognize add/edit/remove/set-default and ensure selected active record belongs to current customer. For add/edit, validate required location fields/format; prototype requires address line, city and four-digit postal code. Maintain labels without inventing a unique-label requirement. Default/remove do not require entering address fields again. Recheck latest saved record and access; unavailable/stale record must not silently recreate another address. Label-only edit can reuse still-valid existing location validation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Valid_35" name="Request and applicable input valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_10</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="InputError_35" name="Explain invalid input or record conflict; retain saved values">
      <bpmn:documentation>Identify incorrect/missing fields, unsupported action or missing/not-owned/stale target. No saved changes. Customer may start a corrected submission; malicious target IDs cannot access another address.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="LocationChanged_35" name="New or changed delivery location?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Add/new or changed location requires Maps support; set-default/remove/label-only edit of valid saved location bypasses new Maps request. Reuse valid location only if its data is unchanged.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="MapsLookup_35" name="Search and validate the proposed address through Google Maps">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-ADDR-04. Provide address-search/location support and validate the customer’s proposed location. Return validated location/address information, invalid location requiring correction, or provider unavailable/timeout/error. Do not infer validation from static preview, treat unavailable provider as a valid address, or invent autocomplete fields/API details. Returned location must correspond to customer input; do not silently replace with a different destination. This does not check courier service area, request Lalamove fees or book a courier.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="MapsResult_35" name="Maps address-validation result?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_18</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="LocationError_35" name="Show invalid location and request address correction">
      <bpmn:documentation>Keep saved addresses and the default unchanged. Return to Add/edit so the customer can correct and resubmit the proposed address.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="MapsError_35" name="Explain Maps unavailability; keep saved book for safe retry">
      <bpmn:documentation>NFR-REL-01-04. Provider timeout/failure is distinct from invalid address. Do not save new/changed unvalidated location or corrupt existing book/default. Retry safely later; no automatic retry count/delay is invented. Default/remove operations can be requested separately without a new Maps validation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="MapsPending_35" name="Retry declined; saved addresses unchanged">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_RetryNo</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Save_35" name="Apply address action and update details">
      <bpmn:documentation>Recheck authentication/record ownership and current address state at commit. Add creates a distinct record linked to customer; edit updates only selected record; remove makes it unavailable for future selection (prototype archives); set-default selects one owned active record and clears previous default. For location writes require current valid Maps result matching this draft. Save requested change and related default changes consistently; first/remaining default fallback follows documented prototype policy. Setting same default or replaying a successful request must not duplicate records. On conflict/failure preserve current saved state, including newer independent changes. Keep historical transaction address snapshots and confirmed subscription address unchanged; no order/delivery mutation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_21</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Saved_35" name="Address/default change saved?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_21</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_22</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_24</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="SaveError_35" name="Explain conflict/save failure; retain latest saved addresses/default">
      <bpmn:documentation>No partial address or default update. Preserve current saved values and refresh/review before a safe fresh attempt. A matching successful operation reuses its result rather than creating duplicate address records. No automatic change to customer purchases.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="SaveEnd_35" name="Change not saved by this attempt; review/retry">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_23</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Show_35" name="Display updated own address book, labels and default">
      <bpmn:documentation>Show active multiple address records/default or empty book after last removal. Refresh affected unconfirmed draft selections as needed; show saved result without rewriting existing paid purchase snapshots. FR-ADDR-05 reuse occurs when a separate purchase selects an address via BPMN-02, with courier eligibility rechecked in BPMN-18.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_24</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_35" name="Updated address details viewed">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_ViewEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ChooseMapsRetry_35" name="Choose whether to retry address validation">
      <bpmn:documentation>The customer chooses to return to address editing or leave after Google Maps is unavailable.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_RetryChoice</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="RetryMaps_35" name="Retry address validation?" default="Flow_35_RetryNo">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_RetryChoice</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_RetryYes</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_RetryNo</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ViewUpdated_35" name="View and confirm updated address details">
      <bpmn:documentation>The customer reviews the saved result, including the default if applicable. The change is already saved.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_35_25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_35_ViewEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_1" sourceRef="Start_35" targetRef="Load_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_2" sourceRef="Load_35" targetRef="Edit_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_6" sourceRef="Edit_35" targetRef="Confirm_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_7" sourceRef="Confirm_35" targetRef="Cancel_35" name="No / leave" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_8" sourceRef="Confirm_35" targetRef="Validate_35" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_9" sourceRef="Validate_35" targetRef="Valid_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_10" sourceRef="Valid_35" targetRef="InputError_35" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_11" sourceRef="InputError_35" targetRef="Edit_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_12" sourceRef="Valid_35" targetRef="LocationChanged_35" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_13" sourceRef="LocationChanged_35" targetRef="MapsLookup_35" name="Yes — add/change location" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_14" sourceRef="LocationChanged_35" targetRef="Save_35" name="No — default/remove/label only" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_15" sourceRef="MapsLookup_35" targetRef="MapsResult_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_16" sourceRef="MapsResult_35" targetRef="LocationError_35" name="Invalid location" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_17" sourceRef="LocationError_35" targetRef="Edit_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_18" sourceRef="MapsResult_35" targetRef="MapsError_35" name="Unavailable / timeout" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_19" sourceRef="MapsError_35" targetRef="ChooseMapsRetry_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_20" sourceRef="MapsResult_35" targetRef="Save_35" name="Valid location" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_21" sourceRef="Save_35" targetRef="Saved_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_22" sourceRef="Saved_35" targetRef="SaveError_35" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_23" sourceRef="SaveError_35" targetRef="SaveEnd_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_24" sourceRef="Saved_35" targetRef="Show_35" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_25" sourceRef="Show_35" targetRef="ViewUpdated_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_RetryChoice" sourceRef="ChooseMapsRetry_35" targetRef="RetryMaps_35" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_RetryYes" sourceRef="RetryMaps_35" targetRef="Edit_35" name="Yes">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">customerChoosesRetry</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_RetryNo" sourceRef="RetryMaps_35" targetRef="MapsPending_35" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_35_ViewEnd" sourceRef="ViewUpdated_35" targetRef="End_35" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="InputRules_35">
      <bpmn:text>Input/access rules
Use only this customer’s selected saved record.
Add/edit: applicable address fields and label.
Default/remove: existing owned active record.
Multiple saved addresses remain separate.
Do not invent unique labels, maximum address counts or approval steps.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_InputRules_35" sourceRef="Validate_35" targetRef="InputRules_35" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="MapsRules_35">
      <bpmn:text>Maps versus courier eligibility
Search and validate new/changed location through Maps.
Invalid location and provider unavailability are different outcomes.
Default/remove/label-only change needs no new location lookup.
BPMN-18 separately checks courier service area/fees during purchase.
Saving ≠ courier eligibility.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_MapsRules_35" sourceRef="MapsLookup_35" targetRef="MapsRules_35" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="ActionRules_35">
      <bpmn:text>Requested save action
Add: create a separate labeled address.
Edit: update selected saved record.
Remove: unavailable for future selection.
Set default: choose one active owned address.
Default changes save with address change.
Prototype: first address defaults; removing default selects another remaining active address; no addresses means no default.
Confirmed purchases retain their saved delivery details.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_ActionRules_35" sourceRef="Save_35" targetRef="ActionRules_35" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Reuse_35">
      <bpmn:text>Reuse boundaries
BPMN-26: sign-in precondition.
BPMN-02: select saved address during applicable purchase.
BPMN-18: courier eligibility/fee check.
These processes are referenced, not called during address maintenance.
FR-ADDR-05 is enabled by the saved book; no checkout is started here.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Reuse_35" sourceRef="Show_35" targetRef="Reuse_35" associationDirection="None" />
  </bpmn:process>
